      "finding": "9/11 folds early-stopped with best_epoch=0 (validation AUROC peaked after the first epoch and never recovered across 20 more), vs. baseline best_epoch ranging 6-54 across all 11 folds, never 0.",
      "root_cause_check": "Verified via a per-epoch diagnostic re-run of fold 0: training loss falls smoothly (271 -> 15 over 40 epochs) while validation AUROC degrades monotonically from 0.64 (epoch 0) to ~0.13-0.20 (epoch 30-39) -- classic overfitting, not attention collapse. Attention weights stay near-uniform across zones (~0.04-0.13 vs. uniform 1/16=0.0625) throughout training, ruling out degenerate single-zone collapse as the cause.",
      "interpretation": "In this extreme low-data regime (11 independent clips), the added ZoneAttention layer (despite only 5 extra params) measurably speeds up overfitting relative to baseline, so in most folds the reported zone_attention_lstm AUROC reflects an undertrained epoch-0-ish checkpoint rather than a converged model. The common-subset AUROC deltas vs. baseline (k0=-0.0275, k30=+0.0456, k60=+0.0275, k90=-0.1206) are confounded by this training-dynamics difference and should not be read as evidence for or against the attention mechanism itself without further work (e.g. lower LR / more regularization for this variant)."
